From 3999ee3b097df375555a404c9c29cf076c688af7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergio Ponguta <sergioponguta@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:06:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kovalla): add a cache chip row and shrink the quality
 chips
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Third row under the addon chips (All, Cached, Direct, Not cached) filters the list by how the source plays.
- Cached = debrid cache hit; Direct = direct playback with no cache label, such as MoviePlus; Not cached = torrent that needs a download/resolve.
- Reads the cache markers addons put in the visible text ([TB ⚡]/[TB ⏳], ⚡Ready/❌ Not Ready) because direct addons do not fill the structured debrid fields.
- Options of the quality row and the cache row are computed against each other, so a choice never empties the list; a filter that stops being available falls back to All.
- Down from the addon chips reaches quality, then cache; up from the list lands on the nearest visible row.
- Quality and cache chips use a compact 24 dp chip instead of the 32 dp TV FilterChip, with tighter spacing and a 32 dp row instead of 56 dp.
- Unit coverage for the cache buckets, the text markers and the quality filter.
